From e08e46aabd21f52dca062479b01fba186fdee433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sriram R <quic_srirrama@quicinc.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Sep 2022 08:39:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: add 11be Single link operation support

As MLD operation for a AP is mandatory as per
ieee80211-be std, include support for handling
single link operation as part of Multi link support

This is basically a stripped off version of a
MLO support with support and infrastructure for
handling ML IEs which are minimally required for
a AP to operate as a MLD and support single link
operation.

To keep the changes minimal, the sta object uses
mld address as its address and link address is
additionally included for any operation required
specifically, but assumption is hostapd and cfg80211.
mac80211 will operate using mld address and assumes
driver performs the link<->mld address conversion
properly.

Security and MBSSID changes will be done separately.

Signed-off-by: Sriram R <quic_srirrama@quicinc.com>
